tree-sitter's C library retains its MIT license in LICENSE. Its bundled
Unicode headers retain the complete notices in unicode-LICENSE.

0001-pyxis-endian.patch modifies lib/src/portable/endian.h, whose upstream
notice dedicates it to the public domain with BSD, MIT and Apache license
alternatives. The patch retains those terms and uses compiler byte-order
definitions and byte-swap builtins for Pyxis.

The build uses the upstream C amalgamation and real SDK libc APIs. It omits
Wasm, parser modules, shared libraries, the CLI and upstream tests. The exact
archive pin, checksum and profile are recorded in share/tree-sitter/source.txt.
